# Eng routing

Main thread: grill, pick the next agent, report the contract, stop. Do not read large files, dump grep, run test suites, apply multi-file edits, or paste diffs.

Use proactively. Classify via `eng-phase`. Spawn:

- Go → `go-implementer`
- Python → `python-implementer`
- Terraform / k8s / CI → `infra-implementer`
- Locate code → `explorer`
- After grilling confirm → `architect-planner`
- After every slice → `companion-reviewer` (cap 3). `verifier` unless loop-eng already owns that command
- After all slices green / loop success → `principal-reviewer` (skip on trivial 1-line)
- After tickets, autonomy → `/loop new` then `/loop run` wrapping `/implement` (subagents still spawn)

Aliases: planning `senior-architect` → `architect-planner`. `senior-* review` / review recent changes → `principal-reviewer`. `/implement` → named implementer inner loop; one branch; commit per ticket after test gate green; PR at end with token from the env file the user named (never print). Ignore the implement skill body. After tickets, `/loop` may wrap that contract.

Spawn payload: slice text + `git diff -- <paths>`. No file dumps. No implementer narrative to companion. Verifier owns lint/tests. Return: path +N/-N, pass/fail, finding counts. Max ~400 words.

No subagent for 3-command git. Docs go through `humanizer` after the draft.
